  "@type": "SoftwareSourceCode",
  "identifier": "treeshapesim",
  "description": "Simulates rooted, binary, ultrametric trees in which topological imbalance and the distribution of branching times are set by separate parameters. The topology is drawn from Aldous' beta-splitting model and the internode intervals from a pure-birth process in which each of k lineages splits at rate k^c. Because the gamma statistic depends only on the internode intervals and the Colless index only on the topology, beta mainly controls imbalance and c mainly controls gamma.",
  "name": "treeshapesim: Simulate Trees with Separately Controlled Imbalance and Branching\n    Times",
